/-!
# Kissat legacy audit: retired `D-Full M4` AAPCS64 AArch64 machine-code theorems

Standalone legacy audit restating, with every hypothesis and postcondition written out in full
(no wrapper `abbrev`s introduced here), the end-to-end theorems about the **AArch64 machine code**
that `LeanQbe.T` emits for the graduated `D-Full M4` Kissat build (`kissat_solve_bytes`, `231`
functions). It imports `Kraken.AArch64` only (never `Kraken.X64`);
`KissatM4LegacyAuditX64.lean` is the x86-64 mirror.

* **`D-Full M4`** (`LeanQbe.T.Arm64.KissatM4`, `231` fns): **SAT (`10`) and UNSAT (`20`)**
  soundness + both arbitrary-host and closed concrete-host (`kissatM4_compiled_arm64.host`)
  non-vacuity, unconditional.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

public section

open Std.Sat
open LeanQbe.T LeanQbe.T.Examples.LratBytes LeanQbe.T.Examples.Kissat
open LeanQbe.T.Examples.Kissat.Full (fullAlignPad)
